pulsar @ 8576283da4ad: make PulsarTestContext compile under Lombok 1.18.48.

Applied by `catalogue.py obtain` and `clean` after the checkout is at source.rev (declared in
catalogue/pulsar.yml, source.patches). Remove it, and the declaration, when the pin moves past a
pulsar commit that does the same.

WHY. JDK 27 removed com.sun.tools.javac.tree.EndPosTable, so every Lombok up to 1.18.46 dies on it
and vendor-libraries.py replaces it there with 1.18.48 (the oldest Lombok that runs on 27). 1.18.48
rejects the one construct below, which earlier versions accepted:

  PulsarTestContext.java:138: error: builderClassName cannot be "Builder" when using @Builder;
  use @lombok.Builder or choose another builder class name.

javac then reports the Lombok round as failed, maddi falls back to parsing without Lombok, and the
@Builder/@Getter members of PulsarTestContext go missing: TestCycleMeasurementRatchetPulsar lost
types and failed on the Mac (JDK 27), 2026-10-03.

THE EDIT is the one Lombok's message asks for, and the one pulsar already uses next door
(SpyConfig.java:40, `@lombok.Builder(builderClassName = "Builder", toBuilder = true)`): drop the
import, qualify the annotation. Same annotation, same generated code; neutral under 1.18.42/46 on
JDK 24 and 26 (checked on a reduced reproduction), so the patch is applied on every machine and
the corpus is the same tree everywhere.

